


   =====( Poll V1.00 ===)=============================================


        Trion 'Poll' Utility.

        (c) Copyright Paul Spijkerman, '94-'97. All rights reserved.

        Written for use with the Trion BBS package.


   ===================================================================


   When you want to make a mail call too an other system with
   the Trion utility, the Caller Utility or from the GUI screen
   in the BBS you have to make sure there is mail for the
   other system or the BBS won't call out.

   This is done so it can't call a number of times when there
   was already a good connect and mail was transferred.

   Also it is use with ZModem in the mailer, if there is a
   session between two mailers and the ZModem file transer protocol
   is used then it is necessary to have files to transfer, because
   ZModem has no option to send 'no files'. If there are no
   files to send poll is used to make an empty mail packet
   for the other system.
   Note that nothing will break if there is nothing to send but
   the systems will take a little time before they go further
   with the session.

   The poll Utility is used by typing poll in the shell with
   a node number on the command line.

   If there is no mail for the system you want to poll the
   utility will make an empty mail packet of 60 bytes
   with the correct password and nodenumbers.

   So if you have a poll script you have to have a poll line
   in it .. but only if you want to call that system also
   if there is no mail for that system.

   Look at the PollHub and MayPoll scripts in the Trion:scripts/
   directory for examples.
   Also look in the Caller and Trion doc for more information
   on how to poll an other system from a shell or script.

   The utility finds the information which password to use
   in the Trion:cfg/systems.cfg configuration file.


